@VC2000-g6q In 925 AD the Kingdom of Croatia was recognised by the Pope in Rome. In 925 AD "Raska" later renamed to Serbia was a region of Bulgaria, ruled by Simeon I of Bulgaria. So Croatia & Bulgaria were then next-door neighbours. The border was the River Drina.
There was no Serbs (or muslims)  living in Bosnia before the Ottoman Turkish invasion which started in 1463 AD. 
The Serbs & the Orthodox non-Slavic nomadic Vlach herders ( from Wallachia) arrived in Bosnia after the Ottoman Turkish invasion.
